Subject: set StartupWMClass to the Wayland app_id org.kde.dragonplayer

Dragon sets its desktop file name, and so its app_id, to
org.kde.dragonplayer; upstream's class names no window Dragon opens.

--- a/misc/org.kde.dragonplayer.desktop
+++ b/misc/org.kde.dragonplayer.desktop
@@ -163,6 +163,6 @@
 Exec=dragon %u
 MimeType=video/ogg;video/x-theora+ogg;video/x-ogm+ogg;video/x-ms-wmv;video/x-msvideo;video/x-ms-asf;video/x-matroska;video/mpeg;video/avi;video/quicktime;video/vnd.rn-realvideo;video/x-flic;video/mp4;video/x-flv;video/webm;
 Categories=Qt;KDE;AudioVideo;Video;Player;
-StartupWMClass=dragonplayer
+StartupWMClass=org.kde.dragonplayer
 # route the rest through kio-fuse
 X-KDE-Protocols=http;https;
